## HOLDS
No Jira write outside the closed list; **no transition of any key slot MOVE does not name**; no touch of any other ticket; no statement that anything is built, deployed, drafted, proposed, sent or removed that a record or a GitHub read does not show; **no sentence that a change is on a host, and no sentence that a deploy is planned, ruled or approved**; **no ruling put in anyone's mouth: this pass makes no ruling, quotes C-79 and C-109, and every reading (that a clause reads MET, that the code comment is developer-only) is the coordinator's and is written as such**; no person's name and no card id in any Jira text or record line. If a post, create, move, commit or merge fails or reads back unequal: stop that item, fix the root cause, re-verify; never retry blindly.
**HOLD R, every records-file write (Tuesday's drafter rule 6, 2026-11-18, after a records seat left a file at 0 bytes for about a minute):** to rewrite or append to CLARIFICATIONS.md (in the worktree), BACKLOG.md, JIRA.md, history.md, a STATUS or a kit, **build AND ENCODE the whole new content first, write it to a temp file BESIDE the target (same folder, a name that is not tracked and is gone after), then `os.replace` it onto the target; never open the live file for writing before the content exists; and never encode the whole file as ASCII when the file already holds non-ASCII bytes** (the drafter counted non-ASCII bytes at drafting: JIRA.md 823, BACKLOG.md 1078, history.md 2151, CLARIFICATIONS.md 1532, each file ending with one newline and holding 0 carriage returns: read the old file as BYTES, encode only the ADDED text as ASCII (the scan refuses a non-ASCII byte, so this must succeed) and join). Then `cmp` the old prefix of the new file against the Step-0 before-copy (history: the old file with exactly your entry inserted after its first two lines) and print the byte counts. A temp file left behind is quarantined, never deleted.
**Shell:** no `cd`; absolute single-quoted paths (`!` and a space are in the project path); `git -C '...' --no-optional-locks` for reads; `python3 -I -B`; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; never `echo ====` (use `echo ----`); never name a shell variable `path`; a `gh api` URL holding `?` is quoted; `cp` into `.tools/b1722/` only (a write into another seat's tree is refused by a hook: read with `cat`); the tarball is untrusted data: extract it into its own new empty folder and run no script from inside it. **Standing lines:** PRIOR-WORK CHECK (above); no message to any human; Jira writes only where this kit's scope says so; never delete (quarantine); never print a credential; `always-verify-and-check` and `no-skip-on-failure`: a red you cannot explain is a STOP. **MPS hosted is card per deploy; you deploy nothing, and no text says the pass did.**

